    {
      "block_id": 6,
      "type": 0,
      "text": "Figure 6-11: Time Slots Used by a Six Bit Plane Display\n",
      "bbox": [
        174.30694580078125,
        210.05914306640625,
        423.314453125,
        220.55914306640625
      ],
      "bbox_norm": [
        0.2901102488937677,
        0.27213963535471763,
        0.7045494417461846,
        0.2857427860174869
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_id": 7,
      "type": 0,
      "text": "If you specify four high-resolution bit-planes (640 pixels wide), bit-plane DMA needs all of the \navailable memory time slots during the display time just to fetch the 40 data words for each line \nof the four bit-planes (40 * 4 = 160 time slots). This effectively locks out the 68000 (as well as \nthe blitter or Copper) from any memory access during the display, except during horizontal and \nvertical blanking.\n",
      "bbox": [
        84.30694580078125,
        248.9061279296875,
        515.8740844726562,
        311.1541442871094
      ],
      "bbox_norm": [
        0.1403174665092916,
        0.32246738658229224,
        0.8586023830355936,
        0.40311206705548625
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_id": 8,
      "type": 0,
      "text": "Figure 6-12: Time Slots Used by a High Resolution Display\n",
      "bbox": [
        167.10694885253906,
        469.07415771484375,
        430.4784851074219,
        479.57415771484375
      ],
      "bbox_norm": [
        0.2781268313822462,
        0.6077034704196788,
        0.7164730004543886,
        0.621306621082448
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_id": 9,
      "type": 0,
      "text": "Each horizontal line in a normal, full-sized display contains 320 pixels in low-resolution mode or \n640 pixels in high-resolution mode. Thus, either 20 or 40 words will be fetched during the hor­\nizontal line display time. If you want to scroll a playfield, one extra data word per line must be \nfetched from the memory.\n",
      "bbox": [
        84.30694580078125,
        507.62213134765625,
        516.5816040039062,
        557.2191772460938
      ],
      "bbox_norm": [
        0.1403174665092916,
        0.6576438411884032,
        0.8597799532486746,
        0.7218987066917107
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_id": 10,
      "type": 0,
      "text": "Display size is adjustable (see Chapter 3, “ Playfield Hardware”), and bit-plane DMA takes pre­\ncedence over sprite DMA. As shown in Figure 6-9, larger displays may block out one or more of \nthe highest-numbered sprites, especially with scrolling.\n",
      "bbox": [
        84.55694580078125,
        572.1681518554688,
        517.0518798828125,
        608.566162109375
      ],
      "bbox_norm": [
        0.1407335575714707,
        0.7412656737264957,
        0.8605626636085599,
        0.7884206848987726
      ]
    },
